oaneoash
======

Standalone Autotools-based extraction of the FreeBSD sh shell from chimerautils.


Policy:
======

This fork is POSIX-first.

The licensed POSIX conformance suite, run from its private installation,
is the release-blocking correctness gate. Its sources and journals are
kept out of this repository.

The imported yash POSIX suite under test-posix/yash is the fast regression
guardrail used while POSIX fixes land. The imported FreeBSD sh regression
suite under test-posix/freebsd is a tertiary guardrail for accidental
breakage in overlapping areas.

The Modernish suite under test-posix/modernish and the Smoosh shell suite
under test-posix/smoosh are additional diagnostics. Their bug, quirk, and
shell-semantics reports help find portability issues, but do not override
the POSIX specification or the licensed conformance results.

When POSIX behavior conflicts with historical FreeBSD behavior, POSIX
wins by default. Yash behavior and the POSIX text are the main
day-to-day reference points for compliance work. Other shells are useful
as comparison points, but are not normative.


Build:
=====

$ autoreconf -fi
$ ./configure
$ make

Build without libedit history and line editing:

$ ./configure --without-libedit
$ make


Run:
===

$ ./src/neoash -c 'echo ok'


Test:
====

Primary POSIX scoreboard:

$ make TESTEE=./src/neoash test-posix-report

The release gate is the private licensed POSIX conformance suite; use its
journals to classify results as shell bugs, harness/environment issues, or
untested cases.

Faster non-signal POSIX pass:

$ make TESTEE=./src/neoash test-posix-nosignal-report

Secondary FreeBSD guardrail:

$ make TESTEE=./src/neoash test-posix-freebsd

Additional Modernish diagnostics:

$ make TESTEE=./src/neoash test-posix-modernish

Additional Smoosh shell diagnostics:

$ make TESTEE=./src/neoash test-posix-smoosh

Convenience aliases:

$ make TESTEE=./src/neoash test-primary
$ make TESTEE=./src/neoash test-guardrail


Layout:
======

- src/         shell core plus generator inputs and scripts
- src/bltin/   builtin implementations (echo, kill, printf, test)
- src/compat/  minimal portability shims used by this extracted tree
- include/     compatibility headers copied from chimerautils


Provenance:
==========

See UPSTREAM.md for the exact upstream commit and copied paths.
